{# ONE BLOCK QUESTION'S CONTROL — the house form vocabulary, chosen by what the
   question is rather than by which block asked it.

   Six controls and no seventh, because the catalogue names six: a styled select,
   a number with its unit, a yes/no pair, a date, a text field, and the select
   that reads ONE AREA'S OWN list. Every one of them is a rule the shell's design
   system owns — nothing here knows what an incident is.

   AN AREA LIST OFFERS KEYS AND SHOWS WORDS. The option's value is the entry's
   stable key and its text is the word, because that key is what the record keeps:
   a word corrected later still resolves on every case file filed under it. A
   hardcoded animal would be one area's vocabulary written into every area on
   earth, so the words come from the area's own list and nowhere else.

   AN EMPTY AREA LIST IS NOT A BUG AND IS NOT PAPERED OVER. A list nobody has
   written words into yet draws its select empty, with the typed `other` beside
   it, which is exactly what the Lists editor's own empty state promises.

   WHAT GATES SAYS SO TWICE: the accent mark a person reads, and the attribute the
   gate reads — `data-need-answer` on a question asked once, `data-need-row` on a
   cell a started row cannot be without.

   Parameters: controller, question, name, areaLists, need ('answer' | 'row' | null),
               disabled, id (optional — a labelled row passes one),
               value (optional — the answer a form that came back was posted with)
   ========================================================================== #}
{%- set gate = 'answer' == need ? ' data-need-answer' : ('row' == need ? ' data-need-row' : '') -%}
{%- set off = disabled ? ' disabled' : '' -%}
{%- set idAttr = id is defined and id ? ' id="' ~ id ~ '"' : '' -%}
{%- set answer = value ?? '' -%}
{%- if 'select-fixed' == question.control.value -%}
    <span class="fsel {{ question.wide ? 'w' : 'n' }}"><select class="fld" name="{{ name }}"{{ idAttr|raw }}{{ gate|raw }}{{ off|raw }}>
        {%- set known = answer in question.options -%}
        {%- if question.placeholder %}<option value=""{{ known ? '' : ' selected' }}>{{ question.placeholder }}</option>{% endif -%}
        {%- for option in question.options -%}
            <option{{ (known ? option == answer : not question.placeholder and loop.first) ? ' selected' }}>{{ option }}</option>
        {%- endfor -%}
    </select></span>
{%- elseif 'select-area-list' == question.control.value -%}
    <span class="fsel w"><select class="fld" name="{{ name }}"{{ idAttr|raw }}{{ gate|raw }}{{ off|raw }}>
        <option value=""{{ answer is empty ? ' selected' }}>{{ question.areaList.placeholder }}</option>
        {%- for key, word in areaLists.options(question.areaList) -%}
            <option value="{{ key }}"{{ answer is not empty and key ~ '' == answer ? ' selected' }}>{{ word }}</option>
        {%- endfor -%}
        <option value="other"{{ 'other' == answer ? ' selected' }}>other — not on the list</option>
    </select></span>
{%- elseif 'number' == question.control.value -%}
    <span class="fnum"><input class="fld" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0"
                              name="{{ name }}" value="{{ answer }}"{{ idAttr|raw }}{{ gate|raw }}{{ off|raw }}>
        <span class="u">{{ question.unit }}</span></span>
{%- elseif 'yes-no' == question.control.value -%}
    {# The pair a person presses, and the one value that is posted: a button posts
       nothing, so the answer lives in the field behind them. #}
    <span class="fyn">
        <button type="button" data-answer="yes"{{ 'yes' == answer ? ' class="on"' }} {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'pick', 'click') }}{{ off|raw }}>yes</button>
        <button type="button" data-answer="no"{{ 'no' == answer ? ' class="on"' }} {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'pick', 'click') }}{{ off|raw }}>no</button>
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ answer in ['yes', 'no'] ? answer }}"{{ gate|raw }}{{ off|raw }}>
    </span>
{%- elseif 'date' == question.control.value -%}
    <input class="fld fdate" type="text" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ answer }}"{{ idAttr|raw }} placeholder="dd mmm yyyy"{{ gate|raw }}{{ off|raw }}>
{%- else -%}
    <input class="fld ftxt" type="text" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ answer }}"{{ idAttr|raw }}
           placeholder="{{ question.placeholder ?? question.label|lower }}"{{ gate|raw }}{{ off|raw }}>
{%- endif -%}
